From d276fe03566024672c3543a7eff2de7515d59c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:20:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: its values move twice a second, not with
 every packet

While the player information is open, the fill of the queues and the live bit
rates are read from the player on every frame, and they change with every
packet of the stream. A label that shows one has a new text on almost every frame,
the skin marks it dirty, and the GUI is drawn again (the whole viewport, with the
default algorithm of the dirty regions) on each of them: over a Dolby Vision picture
that is the cost people reported as stutter with the information open.

CSampledValues gives such a value at most every 500 ms (the same rate as the
other values of the page, which the window system publishes). The memory in use
was read on every frame as well, by System.Memory(used.percent), which opens and
parses /proc/meminfo each time it is drawn (14 us each, measured here): the page
shows the share that the window system already publishes with the amount.

No layout, animation or text of the page changes.
